e 100 butterfly."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Australia led both medal lists, winning 8 golds and 14 medals, followed by the United States, who won 11 medals, but only two golds. Australia’s men led with 5 golds and 8 medals, followed by Japan and the USA, with 5 medals, and one gold each. The Australian women won 6 medals, as did the US women, but Australia won 3 female golds to 1 each for Germany, Great Britain, and the United States."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/45280"} "Murray Rose"] " was the swimming star of the Games, with three gold medals. On the distaff side, " [:a {:href "/athletes/45044"} "Dawn Fraser"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/45020"} "Lorraine Crapp"] " both won two gold medals and three medals. American " [:a {:href "/athletes/51274"} "George Breen"] " won three medals, with a silver and two bronzes."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5379"} "100 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "29 – 30 November 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "34"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5390"} "400 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "1 –  4 December 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5398"} "1,500 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "5 –  7 December 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "20"] "\n" [:td {} "11"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5427"} "4 × 200 metres Freestyle Relay, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "1 –  3 December 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "50"] "\n" [:td {} "11"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/5405"} "100 metres Backstroke, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "4 –  6 December 1